From feed2596083e2c1d243816875128c212c51ec8d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 04:16:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 49/52] signet: require an ML-DSA-44 block signature from a
 height on (-signetpqblock)

A custom signet given -signetpqblock=<pubkey>@<height> requires, from that
height on, an ML-DSA-44 signature by <pubkey> in the witness commitment output
of every block, next to the signet solution (doc/signet-pqblock.md). The output
must then be exactly OP_RETURN, the commitment, the PQ push (PQB1, version 1,
signature) and at most one signet solution push, each in its shortest encoding.

The signature signs TaggedHash("SignetPQBlock", SHA256(challenge) || nVersion
|| hashPrevBlock || merkle root || nTime), the merkle root taken with the
witness commitment output cut back to OP_RETURN, the commitment and the PQ
push's header and version. It is checked last in CheckBlock, on the same
condition as the signet solution, so that templates are left alone and
ConnectBlock checks it again for every block it connects. The height is the
one the coinbase commits to (BIP34).

Nodes without the rule accept these blocks: the rule is a soft fork of the
signet it is given to. The Ark-0 signet refuses the option.
